    \pard\qc\b Employee Login and Leave Request Guide\b0\par
    \pard\qc (Attendance App)\par
    \par
    \pard\b 1) How to Access Employee Login\b0\par
    \par
    \pard\sa120
    1. Open your browser (Chrome, Edge, or Firefox).\par
    2. Open the attendance application URL shared by your company.\par
    3. Go to Employee Login page:\par
    - If you are already on the app home page, click Employee Login.\par
    - Direct path is: /employee/login\par
    \par
    \pard\b 2) How to Login\b0\par
    \par
    \pard\sa120
    1. On the Employee Login page, enter your official company email address.\par
    2. Click Sign in.\par
    3. If your email is valid and your account is active, you will be redirected to the Employee Dashboard.\par
    \par
    \pard\b Common Login Errors and Meaning\b0\par
    \par
    \pard\sa120
    - Email is required: You did not enter an email.\par
    - User not found with this email: Email is not registered in the system.\par
    - User account is inactive: Your account is disabled. Contact admin/HR.\par
    \par
    \pard\b 3) How to Apply for Future Leave / Future Request\b0\par
    \par
    \pard\sa120
    1. Login and open Employee Dashboard.\par
    2. Go to Attendance tab (monthly calendar).\par
    3. Click a future date on the calendar:\par
    - First click sets Start Date.\par
    - Second click sets End Date and opens the Future Request form.\par
    - If you click the same date again, it opens single-day request form.\par
    4. In the form, select Request Type (example: On leave, Half Day, WFH, Present - outstation, Present - client place, Weekoff - special allowance, Other).\par
    5. Enter Reason (mandatory).\par
    6. If Request Type is Other, type custom request type (mandatory).\par
    7. If the selected type needs time, enter Start Time and End Time.\par
    8. Click Send Request.\par
    9. You will see a success message after submission.\par
    \par
    \pard\b 4) Rules to Follow (Very Important)\b0\par
    \par
    \pard\sa120
    A. Basic Required Fields\par
    - userId, Start Date, End Date, and Request Type are mandatory.\par
    - Reason is mandatory from the dashboard form.\par
    \par
    B. Date Rules\par
    - End Date must be same as or after Start Date.\par
    - Invalid date format or invalid date will be rejected.\par
    - Sundays are skipped by the system for future requests (no request created for Sunday).\par
    \par
    C. Time Rules\par
    - Timed categories allow only single-day request (Start Date must equal End Date).\par
    - For timed categories, Start Time and End Time are mandatory.\par
    - For On leave and Weekoff - special allowance, system saves time as 00:00 to 00:00.\par
    - For Present - outstation, system may auto-pick scheduled in/out times.\par
    \par
    D. Partner/Approval Rules\par
    - You must have a partner assigned.\par
    - Attendance email must be configured for your profile; otherwise request fails.\par
    - All requests are sent with Pending status and go to partner for review.\par
    \par
    \pard\b 5) Correction Request Rules (For Past Dates)\b0\par
    \par
    \pard\sa120
    Use this when you need to correct old attendance (for example missing punch).\par
    \par
    Allowed cases:\par
    - Absent\par
    - Half Day\par
    - Holiday or Week Off\par
    - Missing in-time or out-time\par
    \par
    Important limits:\par
    - You cannot submit a new correction if a request for the same date already exists and is not Rejected.\par
    - Date format must be YYYY-MM-DD.\par
    \par
    \pard\b 6) Best Practices for Employees\b0\par
    \par
    \pard\sa120
    - Always give clear and short reason (example: client meeting, biometric issue, travel delay).\par
    - Submit requests early for future leave.\par
    - For time-based request types, verify start/end time before sending.\par
    - Track pending requests regularly from dashboard.\par
    - If login fails, check spelling of email first, then contact admin.\par
    \par
    \pard\b 7) Quick Checklist Before You Click Send\b0\par
    \par
    \pard\sa120
    [ ] Correct date range selected\par
    [ ] Correct request type selected\par
    [ ] Reason entered\par
    [ ] Time entered (if required)\par
    [ ] Partner/attendance email configured\par
    \par
    \pard\i End of Guide\i0\par
